A mailbox's ring, through which a device receives from it, goes once no
running region, nor the GPU process whose mailbox it is, has it attached;
one whose mailbox closes while a region still reads it goes when that
region ends. Here 40 target regions each receive from a mailbox of their
own, which then closes, while a GPU process waits, so no moment comes when
nothing runs on the device. The process's kernel takes half of the GPU's
units (MERK_GPU_PROCESS_UNITS), so that the regions have the rest.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/Inputs/region-rings-beside-process.m -o %t.O2
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_GPU_PROCESS_UNITS=50 OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 MERK_CHECK_MESSAGES=1 timeout -k 1 120 %t.O2 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
CHECK:820
CHECK-NEXT:7
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 messages are neither read nor freed
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 0 rings are allocated

When main ends while the GPU process still waits, the end's check waits ten
seconds for it, and then only the process's own ring is left: the regions'
rings went as each region ended, and the process's table of rings is in
blocks of its own (runtime/device/device.cpp, Block), not in the arena's
chunks.
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_GPU_PROCESS_UNITS=50 OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 120 %t.O2 leave 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LEAVE --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
LEAVE:820
LEAVE-NEXT:Mercury runtime: 0 chunks of the devices' arenas and 1 rings are allocated

With every unit for the process's kernel, the default, the first region
could never start, as the kernel holds every team slot of its units, so it
is a software error rather than a hang.
RUN: not %gpu-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY timeout -k 1 120 %t.O2 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HELD
HELD: Software Error: target region: the GPU processes' kernel on GPU 0 holds every compute unit that its queues may use, so the region would never start: process.set_gpu_units, between kernels, or MERK_GPU_PROCESS_UNITS leaves it a share of them
